  "id": "electronics.analog-circuits.multivibrator-circuits",
  "name": "Multivibrator Circuits",
  "level": "process",
  "parent": "electronics.analog-circuits",
  "description": "Design pedagogy for the three regenerative two-state circuits that bridge linear amplification and free-running timing: the astable (free-running square-wave oscillator, two cross-coupled transistors or an op-amp with RC feedback, f = 1/(0.69 RC)), the monostable (one-shot, a triggered pulse of fixed duration), and the bistable (flip-flop, two stable states with set/reset). Covers threshold/hysteresis design, timing-component selection, and the discrete-transistor and op-amp realizations that the 555 timer later integrates onto one chip.",
  "timeline": "Years 20-35",
  "outputs": [
    "multivibrator-designs"
  ],
